  "question": "Are spatial maps available for the small-cost singleton opportunities, and how much exact saved data can be reused?",
  "hypothesis": "The single known foreign26link has native cost0.804434, so reducing a scalar threshold cannot separate it from all useful more costly fit links. Absolute compatibility with the old spatial template is a testable discriminator; its applicability must first be measured without neural calls.",
  "mechanism": "Reuse unchanged best-geometric-alignment and own-template correspondence from earlier spatial trials. Remove the inherited exactly-two-box gate. Main ordinary singleton fixed toalpha0.025, age2, predictedIoU0.2. Require at least two old observations for a dynamic reference and three distinct reference cells in the same DIS interpolation domain for every eventual signal and support-only control. This is a new admission context, not a new spatial descriptor.",
  "gate": "Metadata-only readiness: at least5spatially available fit20edges and10historical26edges, no more200missing sequences and1000required views upper bound. Passing authorizes preparation under a separately sealed source/input phase, not full20or a tracking-quality claim. Failing stops missing-neural-data restoration.",
  "next_comparison": "If ready: same causal native-confirmed public-ID mechanism and small-cost allowance for ordinary BBOX, shared SUPPORT-only geometry, IMAGE, R1, DIS, T4/T5spatialmaps, RANDOM and PERM. Fixed previous score thresholds, no26retuning. Undefined scores abstain; SUPPORT measures the effect of feature availability alone. Fit selection and held26quality gate registered before those new scores are opened; no full20on failed conditional criterion.",
  "strongest_alternative": "Additional exclusions from frame alignment or spatial support may remove the foreign link without any benefit from activity. Support-only geometry and a rate-matched random veto are required before attributing benefit to FlyVis.",
  "scope": "Only first problem. No causal map-coverage investigation, no turn-direction-lag study, no core modifications. Historical26is not a fresh independent test."
